{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1788173166297,"sessionID":"ses_fa8934456ffeMwhVt4xNG16hV3","part":{"id":"prt_0576d26d1001RnebBkUjty0IF3","messageID":"msg_0576d2332001d1fUR3j3N9AxF0","sessionID":"ses_fa8934456ffeMwhVt4xNG16hV3","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1788173172126,"sessionID":"ses_fa8934456ffeMwhVt4xNG16hV3","part":{"id":"prt_0576d3843001nbYLVzasOBjhwP","messageID":"msg_0576d2332001d1fUR3j3N9AxF0","sessionID":"ses_fa8934456ffeMwhVt4xNG16hV3","type":"text","text":"The implementation confirms both production nondeterminism bugs: it bypasses the injected clock in `add`, `ready`, and retries, and it uses module-level randomness instead of `random_source`. `ready()` also shuffles before sorting, leaving equal-priority order dependent on global RNG state. I’ll replace those with one injected clock read per operation, injected jitter, and an explicit stable tie-breaker by task ID.","time":{"start":1788173170755,"end":1788173172117},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_03545dcc80cbfd4c016a955b72ac8c87d281d8de4116baa57b","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788173178340,"sessionID":"ses_fa8934456ffeMwhVt4xNG16hV3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_loltMnTDHq1YrjKkDnmXxEr5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py\n@@\n     def add(self, task_id: str, priority: int) -> Task:\n-        task = Task(id=task_id, priority=priority, created_at=time.time(), run_at=time.time())\n+        now = self.clock.now()\n+        task = Task(id=task_id, priority=priority, created_at=now, run_at=now)\n         self.store.save(task)\n         return task\n \n     def ready(self):\n-        now = time.time()\n+        now = self.clock.now()\n         items = [task for task in self.store.all() if task.run_at <= now]\n-        random.shuffle(items)\n-        return sorted(items, key=lambda task: task.priority, reverse=True)\n+        return sorted(items, key=lambda task: (-task.priority, task.id))\n \n     def schedule_retry(self, task: Task, base_delay: float = 5.0) -> Task:\n-        jitter = random.random()\n-        updated = replace(task, attempts=task.attempts + 1, run_at=time.time() + base_delay + jitter)\n+        source = self.random_source or random\n+        jitter = source.random()\n+        updated = replace(\n+            task,\n+            attempts=task.attempts + 1,\n+            run_at=self.clock.now() + base_delay + jitter,\n+        )\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py\n+++ /workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py\n@@ -23,19 +23,24 @@\n     self.store = store or MemoryStore()\n     self.random_source = random_source\n \n def add(self, task_id: str, priority: int) -> Task:\n-    task = Task(id=task_id, priority=priority, created_at=time.time(), run_at=time.time())\n+    now = self.clock.now()\n+    task = Task(id=task_id, priority=priority, created_at=now, run_at=now)\n     self.store.save(task)\n     return task\n \n def ready(self):\n-    now = time.time()\n+    now = self.clock.now()\n     items = [task for task in self.store.all() if task.run_at <= now]\n-    random.shuffle(items)\n-    return sorted(items, key=lambda task: task.priority, reverse=True)\n+    return sorted(items, key=lambda task: (-task.priority, task.id))\n \n def schedule_retry(self, task: Task, base_delay: float = 5.0) -> Task:\n-    jitter = random.random()\n-    updated = replace(task, attempts=task.attempts + 1, run_at=time.time() + base_delay + jitter)\n+    source = self.random_source or random\n+    jitter = source.random()\n+    updated = replace(\n+        task,\n+        attempts=task.attempts + 1,\n+        run_at=self.clock.now() + base_delay + jitter,\n+    )\n     self.store.save(updated)\n     return updated\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py","relativePath":"workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py\n+++ /workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py\n@@ -23,19 +23,24 @@\n     self.store = store or MemoryStore()\n     self.random_source = random_source\n \n def add(self, task_id: str, priority: int) -> Task:\n-    task = Task(id=task_id, priority=priority, created_at=time.time(), run_at=time.time())\n+    now = self.clock.now()\n+    task = Task(id=task_id, priority=priority, created_at=now, run_at=now)\n     self.store.save(task)\n     return task\n \n def ready(self):\n-    now = time.time()\n+    now = self.clock.now()\n     items = [task for task in self.store.all() if task.run_at <= now]\n-    random.shuffle(items)\n-    return sorted(items, key=lambda task: task.priority, reverse=True)\n+    return sorted(items, key=lambda task: (-task.priority, task.id))\n \n def schedule_retry(self, task: Task, base_delay: float = 5.0) -> Task:\n-    jitter = random.random()\n-    updated = replace(task, attempts=task.attempts + 1, run_at=time.time() + base_delay + jitter)\n+    source = self.random_source or random\n+    jitter = source.random()\n+    updated = replace(\n+        task,\n+        attempts=task.attempts + 1,\n+        run_at=self.clock.now() + base_delay + jitter,\n+    )\n     self.store.save(updated)\n     return updated\n","additions":11,"deletions":6}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py","time":{"start":1788173178324,"end":1788173178339}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_03545dcc80cbfd4c016a955b74134c87d2836b8e6398b855a7"}},"id":"prt_0576d3d9b001cujUBvi0BunfD0","sessionID":"ses_fa8934456ffeMwhVt4xNG16hV3","messageID":"msg_0576d2332001d1fUR3j3N9AxF0"}}
