{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788173220583,"sessionID":"ses_fa8934456ffeMwhVt4xNG16hV3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_qite6Beqbr02TDK8qFsIteur","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/out/root_cause.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/out/root_cause.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Flaky Test Root Cause\n2: \n3: ## Behavior\n4: \n5: The scheduler produced unstable results for equal-priority tasks because\n6: `ready()` shuffled the ready list with the process-global random generator\n7: before sorting only by priority. Retry times were also unstable because the\n8: implementation used the process-global clock and random generator even when\n9: the scheduler was constructed with injected sources.\n10: \n11: ## Root Cause\n12: \n13: `Scheduler` stored `clock` and `random_source`, but its scheduling methods\n14: continued to call `time.time()` and the module-level `random` functions. The\n15: two calls to `time.time()` in `add()` could also produce different timestamps.\n16: There was no deterministic tie-breaker for equal priorities.\n17: \n18: ## Fix\n19: \n20: - `add()`, `ready()`, and `schedule_retry()` now use `clock.now()`.\n21: - `schedule_retry()` uses `random_source.random()` when provided, retaining\n22:   retry jitter while making it controllable.\n23: - `ready()` sorts by descending priority and then task ID, without a random\n24:   shuffle, so equal-priority ordering is stable.\n25: - The production package and tests were not otherwise changed; the tests\n26:   directory was left untouched.\n27: \n28: ## Verification\n29: \n30: The requested `python -m pytest tests` command could not run because this\n31: environment has no `python` executable. `python3 -m pytest tests` also could\n32: not run because pytest is not installed.\n33: \n34: As an environment-independent check, all three test functions were executed\n35: directly with `python3`; their assertions passed. This covered stable repeated\n36: ordering, injected clock timestamps, injected retry jitter, and retry\n37: readiness at the exact scheduled time. `python3 -m compileall -q flakyqueue`\n38: also completed successfully.\n\n(End of file - total 38 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Flaky Test Root Cause\n\n## Behavior\n\nThe scheduler produced unstable results for equal-priority tasks because\n`ready()` shuffled the ready list with the process-global random generator\nbefore sorting only by priority. Retry times were also unstable because the\nimplementation used the process-global clock and random generator even when\nthe scheduler was constructed with injected sources.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`Scheduler` stored `clock` and `random_source`, but its scheduling methods\ncontinued to call `time.time()` and the module-level `random` functions. The\ntwo calls to `time.time()` in `add()` could also produce different timestamps.\nThere was no deterministic tie-breaker for equal priorities.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `add()`, `ready()`, and `schedule_retry()` now use `clock.now()`.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/out/root_cause.md","text":"# Flaky Test Root Cause\n\n## Behavior\n\nThe scheduler produced unstable results for equal-priority tasks because\n`ready()` shuffled the ready list with the process-global random generator\nbefore sorting only by priority. Retry times were also unstable because the\nimplementation used the process-global clock and random generator even when\nthe scheduler was constructed with injected sources.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`Scheduler` stored `clock` and `random_source`, but its scheduling methods\ncontinued to call `time.time()` and the module-level `random` functions. The\ntwo calls to `time.time()` in `add()` could also produce different timestamps.\nThere was no deterministic tie-breaker for equal priorities.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `add()`, `ready()`, and `schedule_retry()` now use `clock.now()`.\n- `schedule_retry()` uses `random_source.random()` when provided, retaining\n  retry jitter while making it controllable.\n- `ready()` sorts by descending priority and then task ID, without a random\n  shuffle, so equal-priority ordering is stable.\n- The production package and tests were not otherwise changed; the tests\n  directory was left untouched.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe requested `python -m pytest tests` command could not run because this\nenvironment has no `python` executable. `python3 -m pytest tests` also could\nnot run because pytest is not installed.\n\nAs an environment-independent check, all three test functions were executed\ndirectly with `python3`; their assertions passed. This covered stable repeated\nordering, injected clock timestamps, injected retry jitter, and retry\nreadiness at the exact scheduled time. `python3 -m compileall -q flakyqueue`\nalso completed successfully.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":38,"totalLines":38,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/out/root_cause.md","time":{"start":1788173220551,"end":1788173220582}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0830cad2d3df3a38016a955ba46a2087d2bb51cc5b21a5cdb9"}},"id":"prt_0576dfac5001mvsMiMSzjAe1lh","sessionID":"ses_fa8934456ffeMwhVt4xNG16hV3","messageID":"msg_0576de5a3001vx6v8RTQvN51bU"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788173220586,"sessionID":"ses_fa8934456ffeMwhVt4xNG16hV3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_fcyBlifvC9h6EKzWGvrttdSw","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py"},"output":"<path>/workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: from __future__ import annotations\n2: \n3: import random\n4: from dataclasses import dataclass, replace\n5: \n6: from flakyqueue.clock import SystemClock\n7: from flakyqueue.store import MemoryStore\n8: \n9: \n10: @dataclass(frozen=True)\n11: class Task:\n12:     id: str\n13:     priority: int\n14:     created_at: float\n15:     attempts: int = 0\n16:     run_at: float = 0.0\n17: \n18: \n19: class Scheduler:\n20:     def __init__(self, clock=None, store=None, random_source=None) -> None:\n21:         self.clock = clock or SystemClock()\n22:         self.store = store or MemoryStore()\n23:         self.random_source = random_source\n24: \n25:     def add(self, task_id: str, priority: int) -> Task:\n26:         now = self.clock.now()\n27:         task = Task(id=task_id, priority=priority, created_at=now, run_at=now)\n28:         self.store.save(task)\n29:         return task\n30: \n31:     def ready(self):\n32:         now = self.clock.now()\n33:         items = [task for task in self.store.all() if task.run_at <= now]\n34:         return sorted(items, key=lambda task: (-task.priority, task.id))\n35: \n36:     def schedule_retry(self, task: Task, base_delay: float = 5.0) -> Task:\n37:         source = self.random_source or random\n38:         jitter = source.random()\n39:         updated = replace(\n40:             task,\n41:             attempts=task.attempts + 1,\n42:             run_at=self.clock.now() + base_delay + jitter,\n43:         )\n44:         self.store.save(updated)\n45:         return updated\n\n(End of file - total 45 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nimport random\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, replace\n\nfrom flakyqueue.clock import SystemClock\nfrom flakyqueue.store import MemoryStore\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Task:\n    id: str\n    priority: int\n    created_at: float\n    attempts: int = 0\n    run_at: float = 0.0\n\n\nclass Scheduler:\n    def __init__(self, clock=None, store=None, random_source=None) -> None:","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py","text":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nimport random\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, replace\n\nfrom flakyqueue.clock import SystemClock\nfrom flakyqueue.store import MemoryStore\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Task:\n    id: str\n    priority: int\n    created_at: float\n    attempts: int = 0\n    run_at: float = 0.0\n\n\nclass Scheduler:\n    def __init__(self, clock=None, store=None, random_source=None) -> None:\n        self.clock = clock or SystemClock()\n        self.store = store or MemoryStore()\n        self.random_source = random_source\n\n    def add(self, task_id: str, priority: int) -> Task:\n        now = self.clock.now()\n        task = Task(id=task_id, priority=priority, created_at=now, run_at=now)\n        self.store.save(task)\n        return task\n\n    def ready(self):\n        now = self.clock.now()\n        items = [task for task in self.store.all() if task.run_at <= now]\n        return sorted(items, key=lambda task: (-task.priority, task.id))\n\n    def schedule_retry(self, task: Task, base_delay: float = 5.0) -> Task:\n        source = self.random_source or random\n        jitter = source.random()\n        updated = replace(\n            task,\n            attempts=task.attempts + 1,\n            run_at=self.clock.now() + base_delay + jitter,\n        )\n        self.store.save(updated)\n        return updated","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":45,"totalLines":45,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py","time":{"start":1788173220548,"end":1788173220585}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0830cad2d3df3a38016a955ba46a1487d29e2e27bef5156466"}},"id":"prt_0576dfabf001qmBcbxjTIb0kTy","sessionID":"ses_fa8934456ffeMwhVt4xNG16hV3","messageID":"msg_0576de5a3001vx6v8RTQvN51bU"}}
